    "body": "## Motivation\n\nWith priority scheduling enabled and `max_queued_requests=0`, the first incoming request reaches the full-queue path while the waiting queue is empty. Selecting an eviction candidate with `max()` raises `ValueError` before the scheduler can send its normal queue-full rejection.\n\n## Modifications\n\nOnly consider priority eviction when a waiting request exists. Otherwise, preserve the existing incoming-request rejection with status 503. Nonempty queues retain the same priority comparison and eviction behavior.\n\nOpen PR searches for `max_queued_requests`, `priority max queued`, `zero queue`, and `empty waiting queue priority` found no overlapping fix. #37260 changes retraction admission and #37661 adds runtime scheduler controls; neither handles empty priority eviction.\n\n## Accuracy Tests\n\nOn DGX Spark with the current source:\n\n```bash\nPYTHONPATH=python ~/sglang-work/.venv2/bin/python -m pytest test/registered/unit/managers/test_scheduler_timeouts.py test/registered/unit/managers/test_priority_scheduling_disaggregation.py -q\n```\n\n41 tests and 20 subtests pass. On the original scheduler, the new regression fails with `ValueError: max() iterable argument is empty` for both priority directions. The fixed cases check the emitted rejection's request ID and status, and that the waiting queue stays empty. The existing suites also cover nonempty priority eviction and request cleanup.\n\nChanged-file pre-commit passes, including CPU test registration validation. The regression extends the existing scheduler CPU harness and is registered in `base-a-test-cpu`.\n\n## Speed Tests and Profiling\n\nNo performance improvement claimed. These are direct scheduler admission tests with the existing test doubles for transport and unrelated state. No full model server or GPU generation test was run.\n\n## Checklist\n\n- [x] Changed files pass pre-commit.\n- [x] Existing and regression scheduler tests pass on DGX Spark.\n- [x] No public API or con